1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,020
Ten days in Korea:

2
00:00:02,020 --> 00:00:03,940
Jeju’s volcanic coast

3
00:00:03,940 --> 00:00:06,000
Busan’s seaside temple

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,220
Jeonju’s hanok lanes and Gyeongju after dark

5
00:00:09,220 --> 00:00:10,320
in a clear route.

6
00:00:10,650 --> 00:00:11,730
Here’s the whole trip

7
00:00:11,730 --> 00:00:13,810
from Seoul south to Jeju.

8
00:00:14,916 --> 00:00:17,916
And with four extra days

9
00:00:17,916 --> 00:00:20,616
you can add Korea’s east coast.

10
00:00:21,678 --> 00:00:23,278
Start in Seoul

11
00:00:23,278 --> 00:00:26,138
where most international flights arrive.

12
00:00:26,138 --> 00:00:27,618
Spend three days on the city

13
00:00:27,618 --> 00:00:30,578
then use day four for a trip outside it.

14
00:00:30,888 --> 00:00:33,896
Begin with Seoul’s palaces and traditional

15
00:00:33,896 --> 00:00:34,939
neighbourhoods.

16
00:00:34,939 --> 00:00:38,254
Gyeongbokgung gives you a sense of the city’s

17
00:00:38,254 --> 00:00:39,298
royal history

18
00:00:39,298 --> 00:00:43,042
and nearby Bukchon has traditional tiled-roof houses.

19
00:00:43,042 --> 00:00:46,234
Check the palace’s opening information before

20
00:00:46,234 --> 00:00:47,148
you go.

21
00:00:47,490 --> 00:00:49,087
Leave time for markets

22
00:00:49,087 --> 00:00:51,256
neighbourhoods and a night view.

23
00:00:51,256 --> 00:00:54,679
Myeongdong is one option for a busy shopping area;

24
00:00:54,679 --> 00:00:57,588
follow the three-day Seoul plan to fit the

25
00:00:57,588 --> 00:01:00,570
city highlights together without rushing.

26
00:01:00,996 --> 00:01:02,316
For day four

27
00:01:02,316 --> 00:01:03,456
choose one trip:

28
00:01:03,456 --> 00:01:04,896
the DMZ

29
00:01:04,896 --> 00:01:06,536
Suwon’s Hwaseong Fortress

30
00:01:06,536 --> 00:01:08,056
or Nami Island.

31
00:01:08,056 --> 00:01:09,416
They’re different experiences

32
00:01:09,416 --> 00:01:11,876
so pick the one that fits your interests

33
00:01:11,876 --> 00:01:13,576
rather than trying to squeeze in several.

34
00:01:14,166 --> 00:01:17,646
Take the KTX from Seoul to Jeonju.

35
00:01:17,646 --> 00:01:19,806
The ride takes about one and a half to

36
00:01:19,806 --> 00:01:21,426
two hours.

37
00:01:21,426 --> 00:01:24,206
Here’s the short walking plan around the village.

38
00:01:24,624 --> 00:01:27,484
Jeonju Hanok Village has hundreds of

39
00:01:27,484 --> 00:01:30,724
traditional houses with tiled roofs.

40
00:01:30,724 --> 00:01:32,064
Walk the lanes

41
00:01:32,064 --> 00:01:33,684
visit Gyeonggijeon Shrine

42
00:01:33,684 --> 00:01:35,244
and try bibimbap

43
00:01:35,244 --> 00:01:38,164
the dish the city is especially known for.

44
00:01:38,164 --> 00:01:40,044
Leave room for street snacks, too.

45
00:01:40,578 --> 00:01:43,938
Stay overnight in a hanok guesthouse.

46
00:01:43,938 --> 00:01:46,178
The village feels different when it quiets

47
00:01:46,178 --> 00:01:47,438
down in the evening

48
00:01:47,438 --> 00:01:50,638
and an early walk lets you see it before

49
00:01:50,638 --> 00:01:51,918
the day gets busy.

50
00:01:52,284 --> 00:01:54,323
Plan this as a travel day.

51
00:01:54,323 --> 00:01:58,216
There’s no fast direct train from Jeonju to Gyeongju;

52
00:01:58,216 --> 00:02:01,492
buses and train connections take around three

53
00:02:01,492 --> 00:02:02,904
to four hours.

54
00:02:03,390 --> 00:02:07,150
Check your route on Naver Map the night before.

55
00:02:07,150 --> 00:02:08,310
Once you arrive

56
00:02:08,310 --> 00:02:09,990
see the royal tombs

57
00:02:09,990 --> 00:02:12,410
Cheomseongdae Observatory and the Gyochon

58
00:02:12,410 --> 00:02:13,690
hanok area.

59
00:02:13,690 --> 00:02:16,210
They make a good introduction to Gyeongju’s

60
00:02:16,210 --> 00:02:18,370
history and traditional streets.

61
00:02:18,696 --> 00:02:19,936
After dark

62
00:02:19,936 --> 00:02:22,576
visit Donggung Palace and Wolji Pond

63
00:02:22,576 --> 00:02:25,236
where the palace grounds and water are lit up.

64
00:02:25,236 --> 00:02:26,456
The next morning

65
00:02:26,456 --> 00:02:29,616
go to Bulguksa Temple before continuing your trip.

66
00:02:30,306 --> 00:02:33,186
If this travel day feels too full

67
00:02:33,186 --> 00:02:35,826
return to Seoul from Jeonju and take the KTX

68
00:02:35,826 --> 00:02:37,666
to Gyeongju from there.

69
00:02:37,666 --> 00:02:40,306
Or skip Jeonju and travel straight from Seoul

70
00:02:40,306 --> 00:02:41,446
to Gyeongju.

71
00:02:41,868 --> 00:02:44,328
Busan is a short KTX ride

72
00:02:44,328 --> 00:02:46,268
or about an hour by bus

73
00:02:46,268 --> 00:02:48,048
from Gyeongju.

74
00:02:48,048 --> 00:02:50,068
Split your time between the east side and the

75
00:02:50,068 --> 00:02:51,248
older west side.

76
00:02:52,086 --> 00:02:55,346
Spend one day on the east side.

77
00:02:55,346 --> 00:02:58,186
Visit Haedong Yonggungsa Temple by the sea

78
00:02:58,186 --> 00:03:00,066
then Haeundae Beach.

79
00:03:00,066 --> 00:03:02,626
This gives you a temple visit and time beside

80
00:03:02,626 --> 00:03:04,886
the water in one part of the city.

81
00:03:05,256 --> 00:03:08,636
Use the other day for the older west side:

82
00:03:08,636 --> 00:03:10,956
walk around Gamcheon Culture Village

83
00:03:10,956 --> 00:03:12,816
visit Jagalchi fish market

84
00:03:12,816 --> 00:03:14,916
then make time for the night views over

85
00:03:14,916 --> 00:03:16,736
Gwangalli Bridge.

86
00:03:16,736 --> 00:03:18,816
See the Busan guide for more ways to fill

87
00:03:18,816 --> 00:03:19,496
the day.

88
00:03:19,818 --> 00:03:23,518
Fly from Busan’s Gimhae Airport to Jeju.

89
00:03:23,518 --> 00:03:25,558
The flight takes about an hour.

90
00:03:25,558 --> 00:03:27,258
With only two days

91
00:03:27,258 --> 00:03:29,358
choose a few stops rather than trying to see

92
00:03:29,358 --> 00:03:30,298
the whole island.

93
00:03:30,828 --> 00:03:33,948
One option is to explore the east coast

94
00:03:33,948 --> 00:03:37,088
including Sunrise Peak and Udo Island.

95
00:03:37,088 --> 00:03:38,228
For the west

96
00:03:38,228 --> 00:03:41,828
visit Hyeopjae Beach and the cafes around Aewol.

97
00:03:41,828 --> 00:03:44,928
A rental car makes getting around much easier.

98
00:03:45,294 --> 00:03:48,274
You could swap one coast for Hallasan or the

99
00:03:48,274 --> 00:03:50,614
waterfalls around Seogwipo.

100
00:03:50,614 --> 00:03:53,234
Check the weather before you set your plans

101
00:03:53,234 --> 00:03:55,774
especially if you’re counting on flights or a

102
00:03:55,774 --> 00:03:56,674
ferry to Udo.

103
00:03:57,552 --> 00:04:00,592
Jeju has some international flights

104
00:04:00,592 --> 00:04:03,692
but many visitors fly back to Seoul to connect.

105
00:04:03,692 --> 00:04:06,152
If you’re continuing home from Seoul

106
00:04:06,152 --> 00:04:08,512
leave enough flexibility in your plan for the

107
00:04:08,512 --> 00:04:09,212
flight back.

108
00:04:09,810 --> 00:04:10,833
With four extra days

109
00:04:10,833 --> 00:04:13,077
add the east coast between Seoul and the south

110
00:04:13,077 --> 00:04:14,455
or at the end of your trip.

111
00:04:14,455 --> 00:04:16,290
Here are two places to consider.

112
00:04:17,316 --> 00:04:21,216
Spend one or two days in Gangneung for beaches

113
00:04:21,216 --> 00:04:22,276
Gyeongpo Lake

114
00:04:22,276 --> 00:04:25,636
Ojukheon and the coffee street at Anmok Beach.

115
00:04:25,636 --> 00:04:29,076
The KTX journey from Seoul takes about two hours.

116
00:04:29,526 --> 00:04:34,206
Or visit Sokcho and Seoraksan for a national park

117
00:04:34,206 --> 00:04:37,106
a fish market and seaside cafes.

118
00:04:37,106 --> 00:04:39,466
Give this area one or two days

119
00:04:39,466 --> 00:04:41,466
depending on whether you want more time for

120
00:04:41,466 --> 00:04:43,646
the mountain or the coast.

121
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:47,820
You can also keep the extra days in Seoul.

122
00:04:47,820 --> 00:04:49,340
Use them for neighbourhoods

123
00:04:49,340 --> 00:04:50,660
a bathhouse

124
00:04:50,660 --> 00:04:52,820
markets or another day trip instead of adding

125
00:04:52,820 --> 00:04:54,620
more long travel days.

126
00:04:55,002 --> 00:04:57,882
Use KTX for the fast train legs

127
00:04:57,882 --> 00:05:00,362
and check connections for journeys without a

128
00:05:00,362 --> 00:05:01,942
fast direct train

129
00:05:01,942 --> 00:05:04,842
especially Jeonju to Gyeongju.

130
00:05:04,842 --> 00:05:07,242
A Korean map app helps you compare routes

131
00:05:07,242 --> 00:05:08,622
before you leave.

132
00:05:09,660 --> 00:05:12,560
A transit card and a Korean map app are

133
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:15,140
useful in every city on this route.

134
00:05:15,140 --> 00:05:15,980
On Jeju

135
00:05:15,980 --> 00:05:17,600
a car is easiest

136
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:20,520
but buses and taxis also work.

137
00:05:20,520 --> 00:05:20,860
Travel light

138
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:23,420
and use station lockers or luggage delivery

139
00:05:23,420 --> 00:05:24,600
between hotels.

140
00:05:25,326 --> 00:05:29,826
Book KTX trains and your Jeju flight ahead

141
00:05:29,826 --> 00:05:32,726
especially for weekends and holidays.

142
00:05:32,726 --> 00:05:35,266
Check schedules and availability before you go.

143
00:05:35,688 --> 00:05:39,148
Check the season before choosing your dates.

144
00:05:39,148 --> 00:05:40,748
Spring blossoms and autumn leaves are

145
00:05:40,748 --> 00:05:42,888
especially busy times

146
00:05:42,888 --> 00:05:45,788
so expect more visitors around popular sights.

147
00:05:46,242 --> 00:05:49,482
Keep some flexibility for Jeju weather.

148
00:05:49,482 --> 00:05:52,322
Strong winds can cancel flights and Udo ferries

149
00:05:52,322 --> 00:05:54,702
so avoid making every connection depend on a

150
00:05:54,702 --> 00:05:55,982
single tight plan.

151
00:05:56,652 --> 00:05:58,198
Four things to avoid:

152
00:05:58,198 --> 00:06:00,161
changing hotels every night;

153
00:06:00,161 --> 00:06:02,599
underestimating cross-country travel;

154
00:06:02,599 --> 00:06:05,216
booking Jeju without checking weather;

155
00:06:05,216 --> 00:06:08,252
and forgetting to budget for the trip.

156
00:06:08,670 --> 00:06:12,590
Two nights in a place is more relaxing than one.

157
00:06:12,590 --> 00:06:15,050
Fast trains mainly run to and from Seoul

158
00:06:15,050 --> 00:06:18,130
so trips across the country can take longer.

159
00:06:18,130 --> 00:06:20,370
Leave slack around Jeju flights and ferries

160
00:06:20,370 --> 00:06:22,570
and work out your budget before you book.

161
00:06:22,968 --> 00:06:25,568
Is ten days too long?

162
00:06:25,568 --> 00:06:26,948
Not at all.

163
00:06:26,948 --> 00:06:29,948
It gives you time to see Seoul properly and

164
00:06:29,948 --> 00:06:33,808
add three or four other places at a relaxed pace.

165
00:06:34,770 --> 00:06:37,150
What’s the best order?

166
00:06:37,150 --> 00:06:38,110
Start in Seoul

167
00:06:38,110 --> 00:06:41,170
then head south by train and finish in Busan

168
00:06:41,170 --> 00:06:42,670
or Jeju.

169
00:06:42,670 --> 00:06:46,010
Many visitors fly home from Busan or return to

170
00:06:46,010 --> 00:06:47,010
Seoul from Jeju.

171
00:06:47,580 --> 00:06:50,000
Can you do this without a car?

172
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,400
Yes.

173
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:52,020
Trains

174
00:06:52,020 --> 00:06:54,620
buses and subways cover the route.

175
00:06:54,620 --> 00:06:55,580
On Jeju

176
00:06:55,580 --> 00:06:57,360
a car is easiest

177
00:06:57,360 --> 00:06:59,000
but buses and taxis are also options.

178
00:07:00,630 --> 00:07:04,333
The ten-day route is Seoul for four days

179
00:07:04,333 --> 00:07:05,740
Jeonju for one

180
00:07:05,740 --> 00:07:07,296
Gyeongju for one

181
00:07:07,296 --> 00:07:08,629
Busan for two

182
00:07:08,629 --> 00:07:10,332
then Jeju for two.

183
00:07:10,332 --> 00:07:15,150
Add Gangneung or Sokcho for an east-coast extension.

184
00:07:15,840 --> 00:07:16,891
The full guide

185
00:07:16,891 --> 00:07:19,270
with maps and links for every stop

186
00:07:19,270 --> 00:07:21,538
is free at Korea Plainly dot com.

187
00:07:21,538 --> 00:07:24,414
The link is at the top of the description.

188
00:07:24,414 --> 00:07:25,466
If this helped

189
00:07:25,466 --> 00:07:27,125
subscribe for more plain

190
00:07:27,125 --> 00:07:29,140
practical guides to Korea.

